    <DataNode elementId="AT5G17230-MONOMER" textLabel="phytoene synthase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="P37271" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">Phytoene synthase (PSY) catalyzes the committed step to carotenoids. The enzyme converts |FRAME: GERANYLGERANYL-PP all-&lt;i&gt;trans&lt;/i&gt;-geranyl-geranyl diphosphate|, produced by the upstream |FRAME: NONMEVIPP-PWY methylerythritol phosphate pathway| and geranylgeranyl pyrophosphate synthase, to |FRAME: CPD-12321 15-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-phytoene|. A cDNA encoding phytoene synthase (PSY) was isolated from &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; |CITS: [8016277]| based on the PSY1 cDNA of tomato. Phytoene synthase catalyzes the dimerization of two molecules of geranylgeranyl pyrophosphate to phytoene. The PSY gene was overexpressed in &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis&lt;/i&gt; seedlings resulting in a significant increase of one the phytoene successor intermediate &amp;beta;-carotene |CITS: [12805607]|. It has been demonstrated in phytochrome mutants of &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; that the expression of PSY is under the control of phytochrome |CITS: [9351247]|.</Comment>
